      "content": "It is profoundly understandable that if your worth was tied to external success, the sudden loss of that structure leaves you feeling like nothing remains. When the defining features of your life vanish, the idea of continuing feels absurdly difficult. Since the internal \"self\" feels unreachable right now, perhaps the smallest, lowest-stakes acts of self-care—like simply breathing or taking a short walk—could be seen as necessary maintenance for the shell itself. Please know that there are people who want to help you navigate this feeling of absolute finality.",
